    <string name="settings_faq_1_body_prefix">Open the daily log form on the period date, then choose a bleeding intensity: Light, Medium, or Heavy. The \"None\" or \"Spotting\" options</string>
    <string name="settings_faq_1_body_suffix">" is treated as an ordinary daily symptom without menstrual bleeding."</string>
    <string name="settings_faq_1_title">1. How to Log the First Day of Your Period</string>
    <string name="settings_faq_2_body">• Cycle 1: uses a 28-day baseline as an initial estimate.
• Cycle 2 onward: fully dynamic, calculated from your own real average — not a rigid 28 days.</string>
    <string name="settings_faq_2_title">2. How Cycle Prediction Works (Dynamic)</string>
    <string name="settings_faq_3_body">• Pink: active period days you logged.
• Pink Dot: predicted next period days (check next month via the &gt; button).
• Light Blue: fertile window (6 days of conception chance).
• Dark Teal: ovulation peak (egg release).</string>
    <string name="settings_faq_3_title">3. Color Meanings on the Calendar</string>
    <string name="settings_faq_4_body">A normal cycle ranges from 24 to 38 days. If your cycle is &lt;24 days, &gt;38 days, or highly irregular (≥8-day difference), the app will show a warning in the Cycle Analysis tab.</string>
